Module code after the SUBs whose labels the main module uses (an ON ERROR handler, a GOSUB target). QB64 rejects labels between SUB/FUNCTIONs and the old lowering moved this code into a SUB, where the labels were not found ("Label 'HANDLER' not defined"). QBasic treats it as module-level code: the compiler now moves it in front of the first SUB, so the labels and the variable x belong to the main module. Expected output written by hand from QBasic semantics.
